            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "18469100"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Component of the VirB/VirD4 type IV secretion system (T4SS), which is essential for intracellular survival in host cells but is not involved in the invasion process (PubMed:10940027). This T4SS plays a critical role in virulence in mice and in intracellular multiplication within non-professional phagocytes (PubMed:10940027). The VirB4 subunit is essential for intracellular replication and virulence in mice (PubMed:11988518, PubMed:18469100). The VirB4 subunit probably provides energy for T4SS assembly and/or function (By similarity)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
    {
      "commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY",
